---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, FORM_PROVIDER } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SM Global Accounting Services"
  description="How SM Global Accounting Services collects, uses and protects personal data when you visit this website or contact us."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated: 7 October 2026</p>

      <div class="grid" style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: var(--space-3); margin-inline: auto;">
        <div>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This website is operated by {SITE.name} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;), a business
            registered in India, with its registered address in Mumbai, India. We provide outsourced
            bookkeeping, statutory accounts, tax and related accounting support to accountancy
            practices, mainly in the UK. We are the controller of the personal data described in this
            policy. You can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains how we handle personal data collected through this website, for
            example when you fill in the contact form or email us. It does not cover how we handle
            client data while carrying out accounting work for a practice that has engaged us. That is
            governed separately by our engagement letter and data processing agreement with that
            practice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Details you give us directly: your name, practice name, email address, phone number (optional), the area you want help with, and the content of your message.</li>
            <li>Standard technical data. Our website is hosted on GitHub Pages, which, like any web host, may process your IP address and browser details to deliver the pages to you and to keep the service secure. We do not add any tracking or analytics of our own.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Please do not send us confidential client information, passwords or bank details through
            the contact form or by ordinary email. We will tell you how to share files securely once
            an engagement begins.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>4. How we use it, and why</h2>
          <p>We use the information you send us to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reply to your enquiry and arrange a consultation.</li>
            <li>Correspond with you about a possible or existing engagement.</li>
            <li>Keep this website secure and working.</li>
            <li>Meet our own legal and accounting obligations.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Under UK and EU data protection law, our lawful bases are our legitimate interest in
            responding to enquiries from prospective clients, and, where an engagement follows,
            performing that contract. Where Indian law applies, we rely on your voluntary submission of
            your details for the purpose of your enquiry. We do not use your details for marketing
            unless you ask us to, and we do not make decisions about you by automated means.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>5. Where your data is processed</h2>
          <p>
            We are based in India, so your enquiry is received and handled in India. Our service
            providers (see section 7) may also process data in other countries, including the United
            Kingdom, the European Economic Area and the United States. These countries may not have
            the same data protection laws as the one you live in. We share only what is needed to run
            the service, we use encrypted connections, and we limit access to the people who need it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            If your enquiry does not lead to an engagement, we delete your details within 24 months of
            our last contact with you. If an engagement does follow, we keep the related contact details
            for the length of the engagement and six years afterwards, to meet our legal and
            accounting obligations. After that we delete them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>7. Sharing your data</h2>
          <p>We do not sell personal data. We share it only with the providers that help us run this website and our business:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>{FORM_PROVIDER}, a third-party form-delivery service, which receives what you submit in the contact form and forwards it to our inbox.</li>
            <li>Microsoft, which provides our email service (Microsoft 365).</li>
            <li>GitHub, which hosts this website (GitHub Pages).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Each provider processes data under its own terms and privacy notice. We may also share data
            with professional advisers under confidentiality obligations, and where the law or a public
            authority requires it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>8. Cookies and tracking</h2>
          <p>
            This site does not set cookies and does not use analytics, advertising or tracking tools.
            When you send the contact form, your browser passes briefly through the form provider's
            servers, and they may set their own technical cookies. If we add cookies or analytics to
            this site, we will update this section and, where the law requires it, ask for your consent
            first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you are, you may have the right to access the personal data we hold
            about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict or object to our use of it, to
            receive a copy of it, and to withdraw consent where we rely on it. To use any of these
            rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will respond within one
            month. If you are in the UK, you can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office
            (ICO) at ico.org.uk, and if you are in the EU, to your local data protection authority. We
            also handle personal data in line with applicable Indian law, including the Digital
            Personal Data Protection Act 2023 as its provisions come into force.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>10. Children</h2>
          <p>
            This website is for businesses and is not directed at anyone under 18. We do not knowingly
            collect personal data from children.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top shows the current version.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>12. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
